  "raw": {
    "https://nscs.peopleadmin.com/postings/13518": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Admissions Counselor Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About NSCS About CSC About PSC About WSC Admissions Counselor All applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without sponsorship. Applications received after interviews are scheduled may not be fully considered for this position. We do not accept references or other application materials from outside credential management organizations. Application materials and references must be submitted through our applicant tracking system. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Wayne State College is seeking an Admissions Counselor! Are you passionate about building relationships and making a difference? Join the Wayne State College Admissions team and help future Wildcats discover all the opportunities that await them. In this role, you'll connect with prospective students and families, representing the College at high schools, college fairs and other events, communicate with and guide students through the college decision process. Every conversation is an opportunity to inspire confidence and help students take the next step toward their future. If you're an enthusiastic communicator who enjoys meeting new people, traveling, and making a meaningful impact, we'd love to have you on our team. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Admissions Counselor Nature of Work Recruit and counsel prospective students regarding the admissions and enrollment process. Report and track student admissions information. Includes extensive travel. Examples of Work Performed Meet enrollment goals for assigned target recruitment area. Schedule and carry out travel to respective high schools and college fairs with in the assigned territory, including loading and transporting admission materials, displays and other equipment. Present the College and the Admissions profession in a positive way to diverse populations. Assist with on campus recruitment events and visit programs. Present information about WSC in large group, small group and interpersonal settings. Evening and weekend hours required especially during the travel season. Extensive Follow-Up communication (phone calls and email and social media) Assist students individually and in groups to apply for Admission and address the college admission process. Assist with orientation/class registration programs. Host yield events within assigned travel territory. Facilitate scholarship and financial aid leveraging practices. Other duties as assigned Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or related work experience Preferred Qualifications Strong cross-cultural interpersonal and writing skills. Public speaking skills that include diverse populations. Physical Demands License and Certification Requirements Other Requirements Criminal Background and DMV Check; Drivers License Salary Information Competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience. Attractive and comprehensive benefit package. Annual salary range is $41,557-$51,947. FTE 1.000 FLSA Non-Exempt Union Status NSCPA Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1716P Desired Start Date Open Date 08/06/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Wayne State College is seeking an Admissions Counselor! Are you passionate about building relationships and making a difference? Join the Wayne State College Admissions team and help future Wildcats discover all the opportunities that await them. In this role, you’ll connect with prospective students and families, representing the College at high schools, college fairs and other events, communicate with and guide students through the college decision process. Every conversation is an opportunity to inspire confidence and help students take the next step toward their future. If you’re an enthusiastic communicator who enjoys meeting new people, traveling, and making a meaningful impact, we’d love to have you on our team. General Information Wayne State College serves as a model of success for regional public higher education. Investments in infrastructure and facilities, expanded academic programs and partnerships, a whole-campus approach to recruitment and retention, and a commitment to strategic planning position the College as a strong member of the Nebraska State College System. More than 4,500 students rely on Wayne State for access to graduate and undergraduate degree programs in more than 130 programs of study each year, a role the College has proudly filled since its founding in 1891. Our goals are clear: continually improve retention and graduation rates, provide high-quality academic programs and campus facilities, support workforce and economic development in the region, maintain affordability and access, and manage resources for sustainability. We invite qualified applicants to join us in our important work. EEO Statement The Nebraska State Colleges are equal opportunity institutions and prohibit unlawful discrimination and harassment. Each College has designated an individual to coordinate the Colleges’ non-discrimination efforts to comply with regulations implementing Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination Act of 1975, and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies and practices may be directed to the Compliance Coordinators assigned at each College and identified on each College website. Veteran Statement This position is subject to Veterans Preference. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Conferred Transcript 1 Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation Transcript 2 Nebraska State College System Student Employment at CSC Student Employment at PSC Student Employment at WSC Chadron State College Peru State College Wayne State College To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
