      "title": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Project Coordinator",
      "description": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Project Coordinator Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About NSCS About CSC About PSC About WSC Project Coordinator All applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without sponsorship. Applications received after interviews are scheduled may not be fully considered for this position. We do not accept references or other application materials from outside credential management organizations. Application materials and references must be submitted through our applicant tracking system. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Project Coordinator Nature of Work Performs a variety of professional and administrative duties in support of the day to day operations of a function, program, and/or department – this is not a secretarial position. Assists in program planning and development; interprets, monitors, and analyzes information regarding operating policies and procedures; administers budgets; and coordinates academic and/or staff personnel matters. Resolves problems that have a significant impact on the overall goals of the department. Examples of Work Performed Essential Duties: Process name changes Perform degree checkouts for graduation, communicate deficiencies, and follow up until resolved Assist with transcript articulation Manage transcript orders through National Student Clearinghouse Reconcile monthly National Student Clearing report Answer general and operational requests for information in person, through email, mail, r over the telephone during the normal course of the business day Secondary Duties: Process purchase requisitions and accounts payable Assist with graduation communications, practices, and ceremonies Other duties as assigned by immediate supervisor Required Qualifications Associate’s degree or work related experience Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Experience with computer applications such as MS Word, Excel, Outlook Experience with Image Now, PeopleSoft, and/or TES Physical Demands License and Certification Requirements Other Requirements Salary Information $44,239-$46,000 FTE 1.00 FLSA Non-Exempt Union Status NSCPA Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1703P Desired Start Date 09/01/2026 Open Date 07/15/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants General Information EEO Statement The Nebraska State Colleges are equal opportunity institutions and prohibit unlawful discrimination and harassment. Each College has designated an individual to coordinate the Colleges’ non-discrimination efforts to comply with regulations implementing Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination Act of 1975, and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies and practices may be directed to the Compliance Coordinators assigned at each College and identified on each College website. Veteran Statement This position is subject to Veterans Preference. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you now or will you in the future require a sponsorship to work in the United States? No Yes * Do you have an Associate's degree or work related experience? Yes No * Are you available to work on the Chadron State College campus? Yes No * Please describe in detail how your background and experience would be applicable for this position in regards to your technological skills? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Transcript 1 Transcript 2 Nebraska State College System Student Employment at CSC Student Employment at PSC Student Employment at WSC Chadron State College Peru State College 