    "https://nscs.peopleadmin.com/postings/13440": {
      "title": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | International and Cultural Programs Coordinator",
      "description": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | International and Cultural Programs Coordinator Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About NSCS About CSC About PSC About WSC International and Cultural Programs Coordinator All applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without sponsorship. Applications received after interviews are scheduled may not be fully considered for this position. We do not accept references or other application materials from outside credential management organizations. Application materials and references must be submitted through our applicant tracking system. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Wayne State College is seeking an International & Cultural Programs Coordinator. Posting Details Position Information Job Title International and Cultural Programs Coordinator Nature of Work Provide support to international student populations and facilitate a welcoming campus community in which all students are encouraged to share their individual cultural backgrounds and experiences with one another in a respectful manner; coordinate student programing; initiate and implement educational programs concerning issues centered around marginalized student communities; collaborate with Admissions to increase international students; and, serve as a retention specialist for underrepresented student populations. Examples of Work Performed Collaborate with Director to actualize the WSC strategic goals to promote a campus community which provides meaningful access to all students, global engagement and cultural enrichment, and the recruitment/retention of international students and others who provide unique perspectives. Provide leadership in developing and implementing transition programs for international students and coordinate cultural education and awareness programs, heritage month celebrations, and opportunities that promote meaningful interaction among students and the WSC community. Represent the Office of International and Cultural Programs at campus events, new student registration, recruitment activities, and initiatives that promote belonging, intercultural understanding, and student success. Follow federal laws to ensure international student scholars are in complete compliance to maintain legal status. Collaborate with Admissions to increase international student enrollment. Serve as an advocate for international and cultural student concerns. Support faculty and staff initiatives aimed at integrating global perspectives and a variety of cultural experiences into teaching and learning. Support academic advising for international and cultural students utilizing Wildcat Online and Wildcat360. Responsible for evening and weekend international affairs programming and meetings with cultural organizations. Serve as advisor to cultural and international student organizations and clubs. Coordinate the Wayne Community to friends of international students’ group. Serve as Wayne State College Designated School Official ( DSO ). Fulfill other duties and responsibilities as assigned. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree. Preferred Qualifications N/A Physical Demands License and Certification Requirements none Other Requirements Criminal Background Check and DMV Check. Salary Information Competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience. Attractive and comprehensive benefit package. Annual salary range is $54,952-$68,690. FTE 1.000 FLSA Non-Exempt Union Status NSCPA Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1704P Desired Start Date Open Date 07/17/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Wayne State College is seeking an International & Cultural Programs Coordinator. General Information Wayne State College serves as a model of success for regional public higher education. Investments in infrastructure and facilities, expanded academic programs and partnerships, a whole-campus approach to recruitment and retention, and a commitment to strategic planning position the College as a strong member of the Nebraska State College System. More than 4,500 students rely on Wayne State for access to graduate and undergraduate degree programs in more than 130 programs of study each year, a role the College has proudly filled since its founding in 1891. Our goals are clear: continually improve retention and graduation rates, provide high-quality academic programs and campus facilities, support workforce and economic development in the region, maintain affordability and access, and manage resources for sustainability. We invite qualified applicants to join us in our important work. EEO Statement The Nebraska State Colleges are equal opportunity institutions and prohibit unlawful discrimination and harassment. Each College has designated an individual to coordinate the Colleges’ non-discrimination efforts to comply with regulations implementing Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination Act of 1975, and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies and practices may be directed to the Compliance Coordinators assigned at each College and identified on each College website. Veteran Statement This position is subject to Veterans Preference. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Conferred Transcript 1 Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation Transcript 2 Nebraska State College System Student Employment at CSC Student Employment at PSC Student Employment at WSC Chadron State College Peru State College Wayne State College To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
