    "https://nscs.peopleadmin.com/postings/12983": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Electrician Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About NSCS About CSC About PSC About WSC Electrician All applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without sponsorship. Applications received after interviews are scheduled may not be fully considered for this position. We do not accept references or other application materials from outside credential management organizations. Application materials and references must be submitted through our applicant tracking system. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Wayne State is seeking an Electrician. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Electrician Nature of Work This is skilled electrical work at the Journeyman’s License level, installing, repairing and maintaining electrical and communication wiring, electrical fixtures, equipment and systems in campus buildings and dormitories. Performs varied tasks such as installing conduit and wiring according to building plans and diagrams, installing telephone wiring and computer network wiring, assisting in examining, repairing and maintaining motor, lighting and fan units, repairing and maintaining fire alarms in buildings and dormitories. Direct supervision is received from a technical superior with work reviewed in the form of results achieved and adherence to local, State and Federal electrical codes. Examples of Work Performed 1. Perform the following tasks at the beginning of the work shift, before/after all breaks, at the end of the work shift, and frequently throughout the work shift; check/respond to email and submit/update scheduled Computer Maintenance Management System ( CMMS ) tasks. 2. Ability to learn, and use computerized technology to communicate, monitor campus systems, and record keeping per department procedures. 3. Complete work orders and preventative maintenance task as assigned. Maintain communication with the requestor throughout completion of the assigned work order and log data into CMMS . 4. The ability to read, analyze, and interpret technical data; including plans, specifications, and manufacturer design sheets. 5. Knowledge of safety hazards and appropriate precautionary methods involved in building maintenance, repair and construction activities. 6. Ability to analyze and find remedies to electrical problems within campus building and dormitory lighting, security and power systems. 7.Ability to inspects, repair and maintain HVAC electrical units and systems. 8. Perform repairs to electrical appliances, electric motors, fixtures, fire alarm systems, sound systems and controls. 9. Install conduit, power conductors, switches, receptacles, light fixtures and related electrical items including repairs. 10. Ability to use a utility locator and perform locates on campus per requests from digger’s hotline, contractors and/or campus maintenance personal. 11. Read and interpret City, State and Federal electrical codes. Ensure adherence of facility and professional safety rules and regulations. 12. Ability to operate and maintain public address systems and equipment for campus special events and athletic competitions. 13. Ability to perform maintenance on freight and passenger elevators. 14. Leadership and training of co-workers and student employees. 15. Communicate effectively and professionally with the public, contractors, staff, and students. 16. Support graduation ceremonies and other special events. 17. Snow removal as needed. Required Qualifications Graduation from Senior High School or equivalent supplemented by two years of work experience repairing and maintaining electrical systems or any combination of skills, knowledge and abilities that meet these requirements. Possession of valid driver’s license. Ability to possess a valid State of Nebraska Journeyman Electrician or Electrical Contractor License prior to employment start date. Preferred Qualifications n/a Physical Demands License and Certification Requirements Ability to possess a valid State of Nebraska Journeyman Electrician or Electrical Contractor License prior to employment start date. Valid Driver’s License. Other Requirements Criminal Background Check Salary Information Competitive, commensurate, with qualifications and experience. Attractive and comprehensive benefit package. Annual starting salary is $44,141.00 FTE 1.000 FLSA Non-Exempt Union Status NAPE Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1592P Desired Start Date Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Wayne State is seeking an Electrician. General Information Wayne State College serves as a model of success for regional public higher education. Investments in infrastructure and facilities, expanded academic programs and partnerships, a whole-campus approach to recruitment and retention, and a commitment to strategic planning position the College as a strong member of the Nebraska State College System. More than 4,500 students rely on Wayne State for access to graduate and undergraduate degree programs in more than 130 programs of study each year, a role the College has proudly filled since its founding in 1891. Our goals are clear: continually improve retention and graduation rates, provide high-quality academic programs and campus facilities, support workforce and economic development in the region, maintain affordability and access, and manage resources for sustainability. We invite qualified applicants to join us in our important work. EEO Statement The Nebraska State Colleges are equal opportunity institutions and prohibit unlawful discrimination and harassment. Each College has designated an individual to coordinate the Colleges’ non-discrimination efforts to comply with regulations implementing Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination Act of 1975, and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies and practices may be directed to the Compliance Coordinators assigned at each College and identified on each College website. Veteran Statement This position is subject to Veterans Preference. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you received a high school diploma or a GED? Yes No * Do you have two years of work experience repairing and maintaining electrical systems or any combination of skills, knowledge, and abilities that meet these requirements? Yes No * Please explain your two years of work experience repairing and maintaining electrical systems or any combination of skills, knowledge, and abilities. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a valid Driver's License? YES NO * Do you have the ability to possess a valid State of Nebraska Journeyman Electrician or Electrician Contractor License prior to the employment start date? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation Licensure/Certification Resume Transcript 1 Nebraska State College System Student Employment at CSC Student Employment at PSC Student Employment at WSC Chadron State College Peru State College Wayne State College To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://nscs.peopleadmin.com/postings/13543": {
      "title": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Director - Counseling Services",
      "description": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Director - Counseling Services Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About NSCS About CSC About PSC About WSC Director - Counseling Services All applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without sponsorship. Applications received after interviews are scheduled may not be fully considered for this position. We do not accept references or other application materials from outside credential management organizations. Application materials and references must be submitted through our applicant tracking system. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Wayne State College is seeking a Director - Counseling Services. Seeking a collaborative, mission-driven professional to provide administrative, operational, and clinical coordination for our graduate counseling program while serving as BHECN Northeast Co-Director . This position plays a key role in supporting graduate students from recruitment through graduation, strengthening program operations, maintaining accreditation and compliance standards, and creating a high-quality student experience. As BHECN Northeast Co-Director, this position also provides regional leadership in behavioral health workforce development, building strategic partnerships and leading initiatives designed to recruit, train, and retain a strong behavioral health workforce across Northeast Nebraska. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Director - Counseling Services Nature of Work Provides administrative, operational, and clinical coordination for the graduate counseling program, supporting students from recruitment through graduation while ensuring effective program operations, accreditation compliance, and a high-quality student experience. Serves as BHECN Northeast Co-Director, leading regional initiatives to recruit, train, and retain the behavioral health workforce through strategic partnerships and workforce development efforts. Examples of Work Performed 1. Program Administration and Data Management a. Maintains clear communication with stakeholders via updated handbooks and guides, announcements, resource availability, and direct contact. b. Manages program progress portfolio and assessment systems and provides technical guidance to students, faculty, and guest users. c. Participates in Counseling Department meetings and collaborates with faculty to support student needs and develop ongoing program improvements. d. Stewards residency events, including logistics, preparatory communications, evaluation processes, and on-site support as necessary. e. Collects and analyzes data related to student outcomes, field experiences, and program evaluation to support CACREP Liaison with accreditation reporting and continuous program improvement. 2. Student Progress Tracking a. Collaborates with the Program Facilitator to implement and evaluate admissions processes, including responding to inquiries, tracking applicants, and maintaining admissions data. b. Oversees student orientation processes, including teaching the CSL 602 course, tracking entry requirements, and coordinating background checks. c. Administers testing processes, including coordinating registration, tracking scores, communicating results, and assisting students with testing procedures and preparation. d. Oversees student completion processes, including teaching the CSL 692 course, tracking graduation requirements, and coordinating verification of program completion and related licensure steps. 3. Field Experience Coordination a. Maintains relationships with clinical and school training sites and supervisors, assists in developing new placement opportunities, and facilitates affiliation agreements. b. Coordinates practicum and internship placement processes, including supporting site selection, reviewing student applications, and verifying qualifications for approval. c. Updates and shares resources communicating all field experience requirements and procedures. d. Manages placement creation, documentation, evaluation, and tracking and provides guidance on navigating technology systems to students and supervisors. e. Collaborates with faculty supervisors to monitor student progress and verify completion of all field experience requirements. 4. Help Clinic Operations and Supervision a. Maintains operational oversight of the on-site training clinic, including handling documentation systems and technology, ensuring compliance with ethical and legal standards, and coordinating referrals. b. Provides clinical supervision to counselors-in-training when delivering services in the clinic, including overseeing diagnosis and treatment, reviewing documentation, evaluating counseling skills, and being available on-call for sessions. c. Supports graduate assistant staff by coordinating hiring, orientation, schedules, task assignments, professional development, and performance evaluations. 5. Student Recruitment and Retention a. Collaborates with admissions, marketing, and program faculty to support recruitment initiatives, respond to prospective student inquiries, and participate in outreach and information sessions. b. Maintains recruitment and enrollment data to monitor applicant trends, support decision-making, and inform program planning. c. Works with faculty and the program faculty and the CARE Team to identify students at risk for attrition and coordinate timely support, referrals, and retention strategies. d. Supports ongoing retention efforts by monitoring student progress, facilitating communication across stakeholders, and contributing to continuous improvement of the student experience. 6. Behavioral Health Education Center of Nebraska ( BHECN ) Northeast Co-Director * A minimum of 15 hours per week is dedicated to the following components of this part of the position. a. Leadership, Outreach & Regional Networking: Lead and manage BHECN initiatives in the northeast region of Nebraska. Develop and maintain collaborative relationships with educational institutions, BH training programs, providers, and community partners. Strategically gather feedback from local stakeholders to identify regional needs and efforts to support the behavioral health workforce. Represent and promote BHECN at relevant regional events, conferences, and educational programs as needed. b. Communication and Participation: Actively engage in consistent communication with the BHECN Workforce Expansion Manager and fellow BHECN Site Directors. Attend virtual monthly site director meetings, BHECN programming meetings, and one-on-one meetings with the BHECN Workforce Expansion Manager. Participate in the Annual Site Retreat and other applicable events hosted by BHECN . Support BHECN programming through information sharing of regional feedback and other opportunities, such as serving on application review committees. c. Event Planning & Financial Management: Plan and execute regional outreach, education, and workforce development activities for students and providers in alignment with BHECN’s strategic goals and site deliverables. Collaborate with the BHECN Site Directors to identify and develop cross-regional events and initiatives. Facilitate quarterly meetings with a regional Advisory Board. Manage a budget to ensure alignment with organizational goals, including tracking expenses, processing payments associated with the site location and events, and submitting quarterly financial statements demonstrating informed decision-making. Required Qualifications Master’s Degree in Counseling or related field as licensed Clinical/Counselor or Psychologist, Clinical Social Worker, Licensed Independent Mental Health Practitioner, or Licensed Mental Health Practitioner. Possess mental health licensure and is in good standing with all state/national certification boards, with the ability to attain their Nebraska license within 2 years of employment. Preferred Qualifications One or more years of experience teaching at the college level Doctorate or terminal degree appropriate to mental and behavioral health One or more years of clinical and supervision experience in mental and behavioral health Physical Demands License and Certification Requirements See “required qualifications”. Other Requirements Salary Information Competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience. Attractive and comprehensive benefit package. Annual salary range is $57,789- $72,236. FTE 1.000 FLSA Exempt Union Status NSCPA Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1721P Desired Start Date Open Date 08/19/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Wayne State College is seeking a Director – Counseling Services. Seeking a collaborative, mission-driven professional to provide administrative, operational, and clinical coordination for our graduate counseling program while serving as BHECN Northeast Co-Director . This position plays a key role in supporting graduate students from recruitment through graduation, strengthening program operations, maintaining accreditation and compliance standards, and creating a high-quality student experience. As BHECN Northeast Co-Director, this position also provides regional leadership in behavioral health workforce development, building strategic partnerships and leading initiatives designed to recruit, train, and retain a strong behavioral health workforce across Northeast Nebraska. General Information Wayne State College serves as a model of success for regional public higher education. Investments in infrastructure and facilities, expanded academic programs and partnerships, a whole-campus approach to recruitment and retention, and a commitment to strategic planning position the College as a strong member of the Nebraska State College System. More than 4,500 students rely on Wayne State for access to graduate and undergraduate degree programs in more than 130 programs of study each year, a role the College has proudly filled since its founding in 1891. Our goals are clear: continually improve retention and graduation rates, provide high-quality academic programs and campus facilities, support workforce and economic development in the region, maintain affordability and access, and manage resources for sustainability. We invite qualified applicants to join us in our important work. EEO Statement The Nebraska State Colleges are equal opportunity institutions and prohibit unlawful discrimination and harassment. Each College has designated an individual to coordinate the Colleges’ non-discrimination efforts to comply with regulations implementing Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination Act of 1975, and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies and practices may be directed to the Compliance Coordinators assigned at each College and identified on each College website. Veteran Statement This position is subject to Veterans Preference. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Master’s Degree in Counseling or related field as licensed Clinical/Counselor or Psychologist, Clinical Social Worker, Licensed Independent Mental Health Practitioner, or Licensed Mental Health Practitioner? Yes No * Do you possess a mental health licensure and is in good standing with all state/national certification boards, with the ability to attain their Nebraska license within 2 years of employment? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Conferred Transcript 1 Optional Documents Conferred Transcript 2 Licensure/Certification Nebraska State College System Student Employment at CSC Student Employment at PSC Student Employment at WSC Chadron State College Peru State College Wayne State College To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://nscs.peopleadmin.com/postings/13450": {
      "title": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Academic Coordinator (Crawford and Chadron HS)",
      "description": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Academic Coordinator (Crawford and Chadron HS) Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About NSCS About CSC About PSC About WSC Academic Coordinator (Crawford and Chadron HS) All applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without sponsorship. Applications received after interviews are scheduled may not be fully considered for this position. We do not accept references or other application materials from outside credential management organizations. Application materials and references must be submitted through our applicant tracking system. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Academic Coordinator (Crawford and Chadron HS) Nature of Work Assists and prepares eligible high school students for successful completion of high school and transition to post-secondary education.Creates and provides programming for participants and prepares reports as assigned. Examples of Work Performed Essential Duties: 1. Assist with distribution of program information and participant selection in Crawford High School and Chadron High School a. Conduct workshops and information sessions for students, parents, teachers, counselors and administrators and inform them of program services/activities, objectives and eligibility criteria b. Accept referrals from counselors, teachers and community agency personnel c. Meet with each applicant to discuss student’s reason for applying, interests and attitudes toward education and career goals d. Review applications, confer with the Director and school counselors/teachers and compile a final roster of accepted students and alternates along with the rationale for accepting each 2. Provide program services to participants a. Provide academic support to program participants to deal with immediate problems and overcome academic deficiencies b. Monitor participant progress and coordinate tutoring curriculum for each participant c. Conduct individualized sessions to help participants overcome problems affecting performance and retention d. Provide academic advising in the areas of long range academic and career planning, class selection, resolution of academic problems, preparation for high school e. Counsels UB students regarding realistic college choices and assists them in gaining admission and obtaining financial aid or other needed services f. Conduct periodic group meetings for all program participants g. Along with the Director and teachers from the school, finalize a Summer curriculum, identify student needs, develop a Summer Individualized Education Plan and assist with the 6-week Summer program h. Participate in college campus tours Secondary Duties: 1. Gather and process participant information 2. Assists with the APR , Annual Performance Report 3. Contributes in hiring teachers for summer residential program; interviews and recommends final selection 4. Occasional travel and driving during the academic year. Extensive travel and driving during the UB summer program and trip 5. Contribute to teaching responsibilities during summer program 6. Other duties as assigned by Project Director Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Preferred Qualifications Experience working with disadvantaged populations or youth counseling Experience teaching, training, or counseling Physical Demands License and Certification Requirements Valid driver’s license Other Requirements Successful background records check Satisfactory evaluation of driving record Salary Information $47,000-$50,000 FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Union Status NSCPA Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1709P Desired Start Date Open Date 07/23/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants General Information EEO Statement The Nebraska State Colleges are equal opportunity institutions and prohibit unlawful discrimination and harassment. Each College has designated an individual to coordinate the Colleges’ non-discrimination efforts to comply with regulations implementing Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination Act of 1975, and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies and practices may be directed to the Compliance Coordinators assigned at each College and identified on each College website. Veteran Statement This position is subject to Veterans Preference. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you available to work in person at Chadron Public High-school and Crawford Public High-school? Yes No * Do you have a bachelor's degree? Yes No * Do you now or will you in the future require sponsorship to work in the United States? Yes No * This position requires occasional evening and weekend are you available to work evening and weekends? Yes No * Do you have a valid Driver's License or the ability to obtain one? Yes No * Describe your experience in administration of programs serving the educationally or economically disadvantaged. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your teaching philosophy. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcript 1 Optional Documents Transcript 2 Nebraska State College System Student Employment at CSC Student Employment at PSC Student Employment at WSC Chadron State College Peru State College Wayne State College To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
