    "https://nscs.peopleadmin.com/postings/13052": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Electrician Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About NSCS About CSC About PSC About WSC Electrician All applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without sponsorship. Applications received after interviews are scheduled may not be fully considered for this position. We do not accept references or other application materials from outside credential management organizations. Application materials and references must be submitted through our applicant tracking system. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Electrician Nature of Work This is skilled electrical work at the Journeyman’s License level, installing, repairing and maintaining electrical and communication wiring, electrical fixtures, equipment and systems in campus buildings and dormitories. Performs varied tasks such as installing conduit and wiring according to building plans and diagrams, installing telephone wiring and computer network wiring, assisting in examining, repairing and maintaining motor, lighting and fan units, repairing and maintaining fire alarms in buildings and dormitories. Direct supervision is received from a technical superior with work reviewed in the form of results achieved and adherence to local, State and Federal electrical codes Examples of Work Performed Essential Duties: 1. Install conduits, power conductors, switches, receptacles, light fixtures, etc. 2. Maintain and repair electrical appliances, motors, fixtures, equipment, fire alarm systems, sound systems, etc. 3. Install, disconnect and repair motors, starters, controllers, etc. 4. Analyze and remedy electrical problems with the control circuits of air conditioning and heating systems 5. Read and interpret blueprints, drawings and layouts and where necessary draw layouts of electrical circuits to be installed Secondary Duties: 1. Operate and maintain public address systems and equipment for campus special events and athletic events 2. Read and interpret city, state and federal electrical codes 3. Perform preventive maintenance work a. Exercise diagnostic programs b. Measure, record and calibrate field sensors and transducers c. Measure voltage and other electronic values d. Test and calibrate solid state integrated circuits 4. Implement energy conservation methods by engineering and designing monitoring and control subsystem additions to existing data gathering panels 5. May perform general maintenance on freight and passenger elevators in emergencies 6. May be asked to respond to emergencies on nights or weekends 7. Other duties as assigned Required Qualifications Graduation from Senior High School or equivalent supplemented by two years of work experience repairing and maintaining electrical systems or any combination of skills, knowledge and abilities that meet these requirements. Possession of a valid driver’s license. Ability to possess a valid State of Nebraska Journeyman Electrician or Electrical Contractor License prior to employment start date. Preferred Qualifications None Physical Demands License and Certification Requirements Ability to possess a valid State of Nebraska Journeyman Electrician or Electrical Contractor License prior to employment start date. Other Requirements Successful background records check Valid driver’s license Satisfactory evaluation of driving record Salary Information $44,141-$51,099 FTE 1.000 FLSA Non-Exempt Union Status NAPE Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1598P Desired Start Date Open Date 02/11/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants General Information EEO Statement The Nebraska State Colleges are equal opportunity institutions and prohibit unlawful discrimination and harassment. Each College has designated an individual to coordinate the Colleges’ non-discrimination efforts to comply with regulations implementing Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination Act of 1975, and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies and practices may be directed to the Compliance Coordinators assigned at each College and identified on each College website. Veteran Statement This position is subject to Veterans Preference. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you now or will you in the future require sponsorship to work in the United States? Yes No * This position requires the individual to work in Chadron, NE. Are you willing and able to relocate if you do not already live in the area? No Yes * Do you have a valid Driver's License or the ability to obtain one? Yes No * Do you have the ability to possess a valid State of Nebraska Journeyman's Electrician, Master Electrician, or Electrical Contract License prior to employment start date? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Licensure/Certification Optional Documents Transcript 1 Transcript 2 Nebraska State College System Student Employment at CSC Student Employment at PSC Student Employment at WSC Chadron State College Peru State College Wayne State College To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
