    "https://nscs.peopleadmin.com/postings/13515": {
      "title": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Assistant Athletic Director-Student Athlete Development",
      "description": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Assistant Athletic Director-Student Athlete Development Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About NSCS About CSC About PSC About WSC Assistant Athletic Director-Student Athlete Development All applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without sponsorship. Applications received after interviews are scheduled may not be fully considered for this position. We do not accept references or other application materials from outside credential management organizations. Application materials and references must be submitted through our applicant tracking system. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Athletic Director-Student Athlete Development Nature of Work Responsible for the development, coordination, and oversight of comprehensive student-athlete programming that supports academic success, personal development, and the overall student-athlete experience. This position provides guidance and education on Name, Image, and Likeness ( NIL ) in alignment with NCAA regulations and serves as a liaison between athletics and admissions to coordinate prospective student-athlete visits. Emphasis is placed on fostering a culture of accountability, engagement, and holistic development while enhancing recruitment and retention efforts. Effectively leads the marketing, communication, and registration of all athletic camps, ensuring strong promotion and participation. Examples of Work Performed Essential Duties: Student Athlete Programming Develop, oversee and coordinate student-athlete study halls and academic support initiatives in collaboration with campus academic services. Builds strong partnerships that enhance resources and support systems for student-athletes. Demonstrates a commitment to academic success by promoting accountability, structure, and a positive learning environment. Develop and facilitate student-athlete development programming, focusing on leadership, life skills, and personal growth. Also coordinate with career services to establish internship and experiential learning opportunities. Creates engaging opportunities that prepare student-athletes for success beyond their athletic careers. Demonstrates a strong commitment to holistic development by fostering confidence, accountability, and character. Provide training, information, and resources for Name, Image, and Likeness ( NIL to student-athletes in conjunction with the Athletic Director. Be familiar with the NCAA NIL regulations to ensure compliance with regulations as they continue to evolve. Act as a liaison between Admissions and Athletics in coordinating prospective student-athlete campus visits and recruitment experiences. Ensures visits are well-organized, informative, and reflective of the institution’s values and opportunities. Plays a key role in creating positive first impressions that support recruitment and enrollment goals. Camps Act as Athletics Camp Coordinator including the following: Develop marketing material and promotional strategies to attract camp participants, including flyers, social media posts, and email campaigns. Manage camp registration process, including online registration systems, payment, processing, and communication with camp participant and their families. Provide ongoing support and guidance to camp staff (student workers and coaches), ensuring they are equipped to deliver high-quality instruction and supervision to camp participants. Conduct regular staff meetings and training sessions to review camp policies. Compliance Support Coordinates and monitors CARA hours with Associate Athletic Director and Coaches to ensure full compliance with institutional and NCAA regulations. Maintains accurate records and communicates expectations clearly with coaches and staff. Demonstrates attention to detail and accountability in supporting a culture of compliance within the athletics department. Community/Special Events Collaborate with the Athletic Director with the solicitation and development of corporate partnerships to strengthen external support for the athletics department. Demonstrates a commitment to enhancing attendance for external athletic events by ensuring events are well-organized and fan focused. Assist in the collaboration with alumni and community members to plan and implement engagement events that promote Eagle Athletics. Demonstrates strong relationship-building skills that help expand support and involvement with alumni and community members across the region. Continues to create meaningful connections that enhance the visibility and impact of Chadron State athletics. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree Must have knowledge of NCAA rules and regulations. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree Athletic, Coaching, or Administrative experience Physical Demands License and Certification Requirements Other Requirements Successful background records and credit check Valid driver’s license Satisfactory evaluation of driving record Salary Information $50,329-$60,000 FTE 1.000 FLSA Exempt Union Status Non-Union Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1715P Desired Start Date 09/01/2026 Open Date 08/06/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants General Information EEO Statement The Nebraska State Colleges are equal opportunity institutions and prohibit unlawful discrimination and harassment. Each College has designated an individual to coordinate the Colleges’ non-discrimination efforts to comply with regulations implementing Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination Act of 1975, and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies and practices may be directed to the Compliance Coordinators assigned at each College and identified on each College website. Veteran Statement This position is subject to Veterans Preference. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you available to work on the Chadron State College campus? Yes No * Do you now or will you in the future require sponsorship to work in the United States? Yes No * Do you have knowledge of NCAA rules and regulations? Yes No * Do you have a bachelor's degree? Yes No * Do you have a valid Driver's License or the ability to obtain one? Yes No * How do you support student athlete development and handle retention challenges? (Open Ended Question) * What do you consider to be the primary role of the Assistant Athletic Director-Student Athlete Development and how will your current job skills support that role? (Open Ended Question) * Explain your understanding of how administrative work plays a role in the position of an Assistant Athletic Director-Student Athlete Development? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcript 1 Optional Documents Transcript 2 Nebraska State College System Student Employment at CSC Student Employment at PSC Student Employment at WSC Chadron State College Peru State College Wayne State College To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://nscs.peopleadmin.com/postings/13418": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Academic Advisor (Focus Area in Cooperative Education) Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About NSCS About CSC About PSC About WSC Academic Advisor (Focus Area in Cooperative Education) All applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without sponsorship. Applications received after interviews are scheduled may not be fully considered for this position. We do not accept references or other application materials from outside credential management organizations. Application materials and references must be submitted through our applicant tracking system. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Wayne State College is seeking an Academic Advisor (Focus Area in Cooperative Education). This position works with the Career Scholars Cooperative Education Program and involves maintaining a student advising caseload, planning student events and activities, assisting with student recruitment, and supporting student success initiatives. Candidates should be comfortable leading group discussions, and attending occasional evening, weekend, and off-campus events. Local and regional travel may be required. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Academic Advisor (Focus Area in Cooperative Education) Nature of Work Advises students concerning an appropriate academic schedule, choice of major, career, number of hours that may be taken, probation, and/or suspension. Contact may be on individual or group basis or be made by correspondence. Examples of Work Performed 1. Serves primarily as a Career Scholars first year academic advisor. 2. Assists in the development, sustainability and adaptation of co-op programs. 3. Plans, prepares, and implements Career Scholars activities and initiatives (such as career fairs and networking events, mock interviews, and other programs that connect students with employers). 4. Coordinates and attends employer activities, events, site visits, employer networking and off- site activities. 5. Facilitates career placement services and resources for students including expanding a network of potential employers and facilitating internship opportunities. 6. Assists with cohort student recruitment, retention and development; in-class activities including attending classes and leading breakout sessions or group discussions. 7. Maintains an assigned caseload of students from initial enrollment to graduation building relationships, coaching, and facilitating skill development to support students in achieving their cooperative education and career goals. 8. Registers students during New Student Registration, transfer events and assists with other aspects of New Student Registration program days. 9. Supports retention efforts by identifying students’ academic needs, contacting them, and developing a plan toward academic and career success. 10. Utilizes CSM and Canvas to process and track student assignments and employer/experiential activities. 11. Provides leadership for Career Scholar peer mentors, ensuring alignment with program goals and student success initiatives. 12. Monitors events, budgets, and expenditures. 13. Serves as the department liaison with the College Relations department. 14. Other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Preferred Qualifications Organizational skills, event planning, advising or student activities experience. Physical Demands License and Certification Requirements Other Requirements Criminal Background check Salary Information Competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience. Attractive and comprehensive benefit package. Annual salary range is $51,404- $64,256. FTE 1.000 FLSA Non-Exempt Union Status NSCPA Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1698P Desired Start Date Open Date 07/10/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Wayne State College is seeking an Academic Advisor (Focus Area in Cooperative Education). This position works with the Career Scholars Cooperative Education Program and involves maintaining a student advising caseload, planning student events and activities, assisting with student recruitment, and supporting student success initiatives. Candidates should be comfortable leading group discussions, and attending occasional evening, weekend, and off-campus events. Local and regional travel may be required. General Information Wayne State College serves as a model of success for regional public higher education. Investments in infrastructure and facilities, expanded academic programs and partnerships, a whole-campus approach to recruitment and retention, and a commitment to strategic planning position the College as a strong member of the Nebraska State College System. More than 4,500 students rely on Wayne State for access to graduate and undergraduate degree programs in more than 130 programs of study each year, a role the College has proudly filled since its founding in 1891. Our goals are clear: continually improve retention and graduation rates, provide high-quality academic programs and campus facilities, support workforce and economic development in the region, maintain affordability and access, and manage resources for sustainability. We invite qualified applicants to join us in our important work. EEO Statement The Nebraska State Colleges are equal opportunity institutions and prohibit unlawful discrimination and harassment. Each College has designated an individual to coordinate the Colleges’ non-discrimination efforts to comply with regulations implementing Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination Act of 1975, and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies and practices may be directed to the Compliance Coordinators assigned at each College and identified on each College website. Veteran Statement This position is subject to Veterans Preference. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a bachelor's degree? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Conferred Transcript 1 Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation Transcript 2 Nebraska State College System Student Employment at CSC Student Employment at PSC Student Employment at WSC Chadron State College Peru State College Wayne State College To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://nscs.peopleadmin.com/postings/13529": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Licensed Student Counselor Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About NSCS About CSC About PSC About WSC Licensed Student Counselor All applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without sponsorship. Applications received after interviews are scheduled may not be fully considered for this position. We do not accept references or other application materials from outside credential management organizations. Application materials and references must be submitted through our applicant tracking system. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Wayne State College is seeking a Licensed Student Counselor. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Licensed Student Counselor Nature of Work Provides professional counseling to students on academic and personal matters. Provides individual and group therapy and counseling. Responsible for vocational testing and assessment, program development and evaluation and outreach activities. Consults with academic departments and student affairs departments. May be involved in crisis prevention, or aiding with adjustment problems after a major life event. Mantains confidential records. Examples of Work Performed Direct clinical services – 65% Conduct initial consultations and triage assessments, including walk-in sessions Provide diagnosis and treatment recommendations Provide referrals and resources Provide brief individual, couples, and group counseling Provide supervision for clinicians seeking licensure, if qualified Provide after-hours/on call services on rotation with other counseling staff Clinical support responsibilities – 20% Complete accurate and timely documentation Participate in internal clinical consultation Participate in staff meetings Complete other duties as assigned Provide prevention and outreach services – 10% Provide outreach, psychoeducation, and consultation to the campus community May require work after 5 p.m. Engage in continual professional development – 5% Complete continuing education to maintain licensure Engage in activities for continual professional development Required Qualifications Master’s degree Mental health practitioner’s license in Nebraska. Preferred Qualifications Experience in a college counseling setting is preferred. Strong counseling skills and the ability to work cooperatively with the Counseling Center team and knowledge of a variety of computer programs. Physical Demands License and Certification Requirements Mental health practitioner’s license in Nebraska is required. Other Requirements Criminal Background Check Salary Information Competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience. Attractive and comprehensive benefit package. Annual salary range is $49,462 - $61,826 (.900 FTE) FTE 0.900 FLSA Exempt Union Status NSCPA Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1612P Desired Start Date Open Date 08/12/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Wayne State College is seeking a Licensed Student Counselor. General Information Wayne State College serves as a model of success for regional public higher education. Investments in infrastructure and facilities, expanded academic programs and partnerships, a whole-campus approach to recruitment and retention, and a commitment to strategic planning position the College as a strong member of the Nebraska State College System. More than 4,500 students rely on Wayne State for access to graduate and undergraduate degree programs in more than 130 programs of study each year, a role the College has proudly filled since its founding in 1891. Our goals are clear: continually improve retention and graduation rates, provide high-quality academic programs and campus facilities, support workforce and economic development in the region, maintain affordability and access, and manage resources for sustainability. We invite qualified applicants to join us in our important work. EEO Statement The Nebraska State Colleges are equal opportunity institutions and prohibit unlawful discrimination and harassment. Each College has designated an individual to coordinate the Colleges’ non-discrimination efforts to comply with regulations implementing Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination Act of 1975, and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies and practices may be directed to the Compliance Coordinators assigned at each College and identified on each College website. Veteran Statement This position is subject to Veterans Preference. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Conferred Transcript 1 Licensure/Certification Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation Transcript 2 Nebraska State College System Student Employment at CSC Student Employment at PSC Student Employment at WSC Chadron State College Peru State College Wayne State College To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
