    "https://nscs.peopleadmin.com/postings/13047": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Comptroller Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About NSCS About CSC About PSC About WSC Comptroller All applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without sponsorship. Applications received after interviews are scheduled may not be fully considered for this position. We do not accept references or other application materials from outside credential management organizations. Application materials and references must be submitted through our applicant tracking system. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Comptroller Nature of Work As the College’s Fiscal Officer, the Comptroller reports to the Associate Vice President of Administration and Finance ( AVPAF ) and is responsible for overseeing revenue collections, audit and compliance, accounts receivable recording and tracking, and the preparation of audit financial statement and workpapers. The Comptroller prepares monthly financial analysis for management as required and collaborates with the Financial Aid office to ensure smooth financial operations. This position supervises the Accountant in the Accounting department and manages the Revenue Bond budget and related financial activities. Examples of Work Performed Essential Duties: 1. Analyze and review accounting records, financial statements and other financial reports to ensure accuracy, completeness and adherence to accounting standards. 2. Provide College personnel with information, advice, and training on financial matters, as appropriate. 3. Responsible for preparation and accuracy of the College’s annual audited financial statements, including related schedules and work papers, in accordance with generally accepted accounting principles ( GAAP ) and Governmental Accounting Standards Board ( GASB ) standards. 4. Act as the primary liaison with external auditors for the Basic Financials, Revenue Bond, and Single audits ensuing timely responses to inquiries, provision of necessary documentation, and explanation of accounting transactions. 5. Review auditors’ management letters and implement internal controls or procedural improvements as needed. 6. Establish and maintain accounting internal controls to safeguard College assets and ensure accurate financial reporting. 7. Collaborate with Nebraska State College System ( NSCS ) System Finance Director and the Comptrollers from Wayne State and Peru State Colleges to align financial reporting practices across the NSCS . 8. Prepare financial reports for the NSCS Board of Trustees and various external agencies, including but not limited to the review of annual FISAP reports for Financial Aid, the completion of the annual financial section of the IPEDs Survey and the annual financial information section of the HLC report. 9. Conduct analysis and provide advice on College finances and auxiliary enterprises at the request of senior administration. 10. Research, evaluate, and recommend improvements to financial policies, procedures and accounting systems to enhance efficiency and effectiveness. 11. Ensures compliance with accounting principles, legal regulations, and NSCS Board of Trustees policies. 12. Manage the College’s system of accounts, ensuring proper posting, balancing, and reconciliation of general and subsidiary ledgers. 13. Collaborate with the Director of Business Services, Budget Director, Athletic Business Manager, and other stakeholders to ensure compliance with accounting standards and appropriate internal controls for areas like cash management, accounts receivable, financial aid disbursements, and athletic accounting. 14. Responsible for Revenue Bond budgeting and financial reporting, working closely with the Budget Director to coordinate budgeting and reporting processes. 15. Monitor fund accounts to maintain sufficient cash fund balances and coordinate investments activities. 16. Formulate and administer procedures for the accounting operations, including but not limited to financial statement preparation, general ledger reconciliation, and cash management. 17. Oversee daily cash receipts, deposits, monthly bank reconciliations, and grant processing. Secondary Duties: 1. Assist the AVPAF and Vice President for Administration and Finance as needed. 2. Committee and planning duties 3. Perform other duties as assigned by the AVPAF . Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in accounting or closely related field. 3 years of experience in Accounting and knowledge of preparing or auditing financial statements or equivalent experience. Knowledge of and application of financial accounting standards. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree 5 years work experience in governmental accounting and/or higher education. Experience with SAP accounting system. Working knowledge of GASB . Analytical/problem solving skills and attention to detail. Certified Public Accountant License Physical Demands License and Certification Requirements None Other Requirements Successful background records and credit check Salary Information $85,000-$100,000 FTE 1.000 FLSA Exempt Union Status Non-Union Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1605P Desired Start Date Open Date 02/10/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants General Information EEO Statement The Nebraska State Colleges are equal opportunity institutions and prohibit unlawful discrimination and harassment. Each College has designated an individual to coordinate the Colleges’ non-discrimination efforts to comply with regulations implementing Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination Act of 1975, and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies and practices may be directed to the Compliance Coordinators assigned at each College and identified on each College website. Veteran Statement This position is subject to Veterans Preference. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you now or will you in the future require sponsorship to work in the United States? Yes No * This position requires the individual to work in Chadron, NE.  Are you willing and able to relocate if you do not already live in the area? Yes No * Do you have a bachelor's degree? Yes No * How would you rate your Excel skills? None Light User Experienced User Advanced User * Do you have at least three years experience in Accounting and knowledge of preparing or auditing financial statements? Yes No * Do you have any experience with SAP? Yes No * Do you hold a CPA license? Yes No * How many years of work experience in accounting or bookkeeping? 0 1-2 3-4 5-7 7+ * What have you done to improve your audit knowledge in the past year? (Open Ended Question) * Explain the importance of the ability to establish and maintain cooperative working relationships with a wide variety of people. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcript 1 Optional Documents Nebraska State College System Student Employment at CSC Student Employment at PSC Student Employment at WSC Chadron State College Peru State College Wayne State College To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://nscs.peopleadmin.com/postings/13549": {
      "title": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Graduate Assistant (Strength &amp; Conditioning)",
      "description": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Graduate Assistant (Strength &amp; Conditioning) Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About NSCS About CSC About PSC About WSC Graduate Assistant (Strength & Conditioning) All applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without sponsorship. Applications received after interviews are scheduled may not be fully considered for this position. We do not accept references or other application materials from outside credential management organizations. Application materials and references must be submitted through our applicant tracking system. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Wayne State College is seeking a Graduate Assistant for the Strength and Conditioning department. A total (maximum) of 400 hours of work is required for this Graduate Assistantship. Typically, twenty-five (25) hours of work will be assigned per week by your supervisor during the Spring Semester. The special appointment provides a stipend of $6,300.00 for the 2027 Spring Semester and a graduate tuition waiver available for up to 9 credit hours including the immediately following summer session. All fees will be the responsibility of the student regardless of online or on-campus. Tuition remissions awarded for online courses will not exceed the comparable amount provided for an on-campus course for a resident student. This is an appointment with the opportunity of renewal after the first year. Desired start date of Spring 2027. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Graduate Assistant (Strength & Conditioning) Nature of Work Graduate Assistants are hired at Wayne State College to assist in meeting the vision and goals established for WSC . Strategic deployment of graduate assistant positions is essential to ensure that limited resources are utilized in a manner consistent with the philosophy of WSC . Graduate assistants provide experiential learning in select areas and to assist the individual in a successful transition to future educational and professional opportunities. Examples of Work Performed Programming for multiple sports, leading and assisting athletes though training, overseeing facility needs, assisting in mobility programs, assisting in nutrition including fueling station, overseeing facility during open lifting times, assisting in oversight of interns. Other duties as assigned by Head Strength and Conditioning Coach. Make satisfactory progress on degree program and maintain good academic standing ( GPA > 3.0). Required Qualifications Applicants must be accepted into graduate program of study at WSC . Applying for graduate studies at Wayne State College is now totally online. Graduate school information and applications can be found at https://www.wsc.edu/graduate Previous experience in strength and conditioning. CPR / AED certification or the ability to become certified. Preferred Qualifications • National Certification ( CSCS , SCCC , USAW ) • Previous collegiate strength and conditioning experience Physical Demands License and Certification Requirements N/A Other Requirements Background Check Salary Information This special appointment provides a stipend of $6,300.00 for the 2027 Spring Semester and a graduate tuition waiver available for up to 9 credit hours including the immediately following summer session. FTE 0.000 FLSA Exempt Union Status Non-Union Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1724P Desired Start Date Open Date 08/21/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Wayne State College is seeking a Graduate Assistant for the Strength and Conditioning department. A total (maximum) of 400 hours of work is required for this Graduate Assistantship. Typically, twenty-five (25) hours of work will be assigned per week by your supervisor during the Spring Semester. The special appointment provides a stipend of $6,300.00 for the 2027 Spring Semester and a graduate tuition waiver available for up to 9 credit hours including the immediately following summer session. All fees will be the responsibility of the student regardless of online or on-campus. Tuition remissions awarded for online courses will not exceed the comparable amount provided for an on-campus course for a resident student. This is an appointment with the opportunity of renewal after the first year. Desired start date of Spring 2027. General Information Wayne State College serves as a model of success for regional public higher education. Investments in infrastructure and facilities, expanded academic programs and partnerships, a whole-campus approach to recruitment and retention, and a commitment to strategic planning position the College as a strong member of the Nebraska State College System. More than 4,500 students rely on Wayne State for access to graduate and undergraduate degree programs in more than 130 programs of study each year, a role the College has proudly filled since its founding in 1891. Our goals are clear: continually improve retention and graduation rates, provide high-quality academic programs and campus facilities, support workforce and economic development in the region, maintain affordability and access, and manage resources for sustainability. We invite qualified applicants to join us in our important work. EEO Statement The Nebraska State Colleges are equal opportunity institutions and prohibit unlawful discrimination and harassment. Each College has designated an individual to coordinate the Colleges’ non-discrimination efforts to comply with regulations implementing Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination Act of 1975, and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies and practices may be directed to the Compliance Coordinators assigned at each College and identified on each College website. Veteran Statement This position is subject to Veterans Preference. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have previous experience in Strength and Conditioning? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation Transcript 1 Nebraska State College System Student Employment at CSC Student Employment at PSC Student Employment at WSC Chadron State College Peru State College Wayne State College To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://nscs.peopleadmin.com/postings/13451": {
      "title": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Academic Coordinator (Alliance HS)",
      "description": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Academic Coordinator (Alliance HS) Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About NSCS About CSC About PSC About WSC Academic Coordinator (Alliance HS) All applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without sponsorship. Applications received after interviews are scheduled may not be fully considered for this position. We do not accept references or other application materials from outside credential management organizations. Application materials and references must be submitted through our applicant tracking system. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Academic Coordinator (Alliance HS) Nature of Work Assists and prepares eligible high school students for successful completion of high school and transition to post-secondary education. Creates and provides programming for participants and prepares reports as assigned. Examples of Work Performed Essential Duties: 1. Assist with distribution of program information and participant selection in Alliance High School a. Conduct workshops and information sessions for students, parents, teachers, counselors and administrators and inform them of program services/activities, objectives and eligibility criteria b. Accept referrals from counselors, teachers and community agency personnel c. Meet with each applicant to discuss student’s reason for applying, interests and attitudes toward education and career goals d. Review applications, confer with the Director and school counselors/teachers and compile a final roster of accepted students and alternates along with the rationale for accepting each 2. Provide program services to participants a. Provide academic support to program participants to deal with immediate problems and overcome academic deficiencies b. Monitor participant progress and coordinate tutoring curriculum for each participant c. Conduct individualized sessions to help participants overcome problems affecting performance and retention d. Provide academic advising in the areas of long range academic and career planning, class selection, resolution of academic problems, preparation for high school e. Counsels UB students regarding realistic college choices and assists them in gaining admission and obtaining financial aid or other needed services f. Conduct periodic group meetings for all program participants g. Along with the Director and teachers from the school, finalize a Summer curriculum, identify student needs, develop a Summer Individualized Education Plan and assist with the 6-week Summer program h. Participate in college campus tours Secondary Duties: 1. Gather and process participant information 2. Assists with the APR , Annual Performance Report 3. Contributes in hiring teachers for summer residential program; interviews and recommends final selection 4. Occasional travel and driving during the academic year. Extensive travel and driving during the UB summer program and trip 5. Contribute to teaching responsibilities during summer program 6. Other duties as assigned by Project Director Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Preferred Qualifications Experience working with disadvantaged populations or youth counseling Experience teaching, training, or counseling Physical Demands License and Certification Requirements Valid driver’s license Other Requirements Successful background records check Satisfactory evaluation of driving record Salary Information $23,500-$25,000  This is .50 FTE with off contract periods FTE 0.500 FLSA Non-Exempt Union Status Non-Union Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1708P Desired Start Date Open Date 07/23/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants General Information EEO Statement The Nebraska State Colleges are equal opportunity institutions and prohibit unlawful discrimination and harassment. Each College has designated an individual to coordinate the Colleges’ non-discrimination efforts to comply with regulations implementing Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination Act of 1975, and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies and practices may be directed to the Compliance Coordinators assigned at each College and identified on each College website. Veteran Statement This position is subject to Veterans Preference. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you available to work in person at Alliance Public HighSchool? Yes No * Do you have a bachelor's degree? Yes No * Do you now or will you in the future require sponsorship to work in the United States? Yes No * This position requires occasional evening and weekend are you available to work evening and weekends? Yes No * Do you have a valid Driver's License or the ability to obtain one? Yes No * Describe your experience in administration of programs serving the educationally or economically disadvantaged. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your teaching philosophy. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcript 1 Optional Documents Transcript 2 Nebraska State College System Student Employment at CSC Student Employment at PSC Student Employment at WSC Chadron State College Peru State College Wayne State College To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://nscs.peopleadmin.com/postings/13557": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Maintenance Repair Worker III (HVAC &amp; Plumbing) Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About NSCS About CSC About PSC About WSC Maintenance Repair Worker III (HVAC & Plumbing) All applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without sponsorship. Applications received after interviews are scheduled may not be fully considered for this position. We do not accept references or other application materials from outside credential management organizations. Application materials and references must be submitted through our applicant tracking system. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Wayne State College is seeking a Maintenance Repair Worker III (HVAC & Plumbing) to work rotating shifts. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Maintenance Repair Worker III (HVAC & Plumbing) Nature of Work This is a skilled classification level to perform advanced maintenance and repair in buildings, facilities and grounds. Work involves primary responsibility for activities in any one or more of the following craft areas: energy operations, HVAC , plumbing or related disciplines. Additionally, this classification is expected to provide technical guidance and direct the work of other maintenance personnel in an area of expertise. Work requires a significant amount of independent judgment and advanced decision making skills. Work requires initiative, the ability to self-direct work and problem solve. Work involves extensive trouble-shooting skills; the ability to inspect and diagnose the exact nature of complex problems and make necessary repairs; utilization of advanced preventive maintenance techniques; and, the ability to read, analyze and interpret technical data. Limited leadership may be provided to small crews of co-workers or student employees. Work must be performed in accordance with all applicable building codes, departmental policies, procedures and protocols. Work environments will consist of indoor, outdoor, independent work or as a part of a team. General supervision and oversight is provided to employees in this classification. Examples of Work Performed This position normally works rotating shifts; 7:00 AM to 3:30 PM Monday through Friday alternating with 7:00 AM to 3:30 PM Tuesday through Saturday (Sunday and Monday before off), 7:00 AM to 3:30 PM Sunday through Thursday (Friday and Saturday after off). During the Academic year every 5th week is scheduled 9:00 AM to 6:00 PM Monday through Friday. Schedule subject to change as needed and work may be required during non-routine times, inclement weather, or to support special events. Routine Duties Research and notify supervisor to order repair parts or supplies Maintain work environments in a clean and safe manner Maintain inspection schedules and daily building mechanical room checks Take time at the beginning of the shift, near breaks, and at the end of the shift to check the Building Management System ( BMS ) for alarms, update Computerized Maintenance Management System (cmms) and e-mail Monitor ( BMS ), determining the corrective actions needed to maintain specifications Utilize building and equipment controls to maintain a comfortable environment Utilize dashboard data, set-backs, and load shedding to increase system efficiency Work with co-workers in the areas of safety, quality, and productivity, with a focus on reliable customer service Operate specialized tools and equipment using advance knowledge Communicate effectively and professionally with the general public, staff, and students Use technology in communication, monitoring, and record keeping per department procedures Troubleshoot and make needed repairs or adjustments to maintain safety and comfort using independent judgment Focus and utilization of preventative and predictive maintenance practices that improve service and efficiency Maintain productivity and initiative while working alone or as a team Other duties as assigned Required Qualifications High School education or GED A minimum of four years previous experience in maintenance, repair or construction activities in an area of automotive, carpentry, electrical, energy operations, grounds, HVAC , painting, plumbing or related discipline. Note: years of “previous experience” shall not be construed as an automatic prompt or cause for reclassification. Must be able to operate a computer and small equipment Valid Driver’s License Preferred Qualifications N/A Physical Demands Employee must be able to work in extreme hot and cold conditions, bend, crouch, climb ladders, and assist in safe lifting in excess of 75 pounds. License and Certification Requirements Valid Driver’s License Other Requirements Criminal Background Check DMV Check Salary Information Competitive, commensurate, with qualifications and experience. Attractive and comprehensive benefit package. Annual starting salary is $42,610. FTE 1.000 FLSA Non-Exempt Union Status NAPE Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1728P Desired Start Date Open Date 08/25/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Wayne State College is seeking a Maintenance Repair Worker III ( HVAC & Plumbing) to work rotating shifts. General Information Wayne State College serves as a model of success for regional public higher education. Investments in infrastructure and facilities, expanded academic programs and partnerships, a whole-campus approach to recruitment and retention, and a commitment to strategic planning position the College as a strong member of the Nebraska State College System. More than 4,500 students rely on Wayne State for access to graduate and undergraduate degree programs in more than 130 programs of study each year, a role the College has proudly filled since its founding in 1891. Our goals are clear: continually improve retention and graduation rates, provide high-quality academic programs and campus facilities, support workforce and economic development in the region, maintain affordability and access, and manage resources for sustainability. We invite qualified applicants to join us in our important work. EEO Statement The Nebraska State Colleges are equal opportunity institutions and prohibit unlawful discrimination and harassment. Each College has designated an individual to coordinate the Colleges’ non-discrimination efforts to comply with regulations implementing Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination Act of 1975, and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies and practices may be directed to the Compliance Coordinators assigned at each College and identified on each College website. Veteran Statement This position is subject to Veterans Preference. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a minimum of four years previous experience in maintenance, repair, or construction activities in an area of automotive, carpentry, electrical, energy operations, grounds, HVAC, painting, plumbing, or related discipline? Yes No * Please describe your work experience related to maintenance, repair, and construction activities. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have the ability to operate a computer and small equipment? Yes No * Do you have the ability to work in extreme hot and cold conditions, bend, crouch, climb ladders, and assist in safe lifting in excess of 75 pounds? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation Licensure/Certification Resume Nebraska State College System Student Employment at CSC Student Employment at PSC Student Employment at WSC Chadron State College Peru State College Wayne State College To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
