    "https://nscs.peopleadmin.com/postings/13236": {
      "title": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Coordinator of Conferencing",
      "description": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Coordinator of Conferencing Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About NSCS About CSC About PSC About WSC Coordinator of Conferencing All applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without sponsorship. Applications received after interviews are scheduled may not be fully considered for this position. We do not accept references or other application materials from outside credential management organizations. Application materials and references must be submitted through our applicant tracking system. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Coordinator of Conferencing Nature of Work To provide assistance and/or guidance for the campus and to local, regional and national organizations in the coordination of successful events (including but not limited to conventions, workshops, social events, conferences, and meetings) held at or for the institution. Examples of Work Performed Essential Duties: 1. Commit to providing a positive experience to all Chadron State College conference clients, responding to requests and fulfilling the needs of the clients. 2. Develop and manage procedures for the coordination of all services involved in conferencing event management. 3. Initiate, coordinate, implement, support and monitor all logistical aspects of conferences and special events for external and internal clients and summer use of residence halls including, but not limited to, room scheduling, housing accommodations, facilities set-ups, contracting, invoicing, coordinating with security, athletics, custodial, maintenance, and college relations departments as well as contracted food service vendor. 4.Coordinate audio visual needs, set up requirements, and effectively communicate contract details to all clients. 5. Respond timely to all inquiries for the use of college facilities, maintain communication and prompt follow-up with a professional proposal including campus information, suggestions, and final agreement compiled in a Facility Rental Agreement. 6. Expand revenue-producing activities located on the CSC campus that directly benefit auxiliary operations. 7. Maintain effective budget control for the Department. 8. Maintain the electronic campus-wide facility reservation request system and provide access and training for various employees to schedule events through the system. This system is used for utilization reports. 9. Coordinate materials displayed on the digital sign at the Main Street entrance to campus and all digital signs located in the Student Center except for dining service digital signs located in the dining hall and market. 10. Maintain up to date knowledge of trends/developments in the field of Conference and Event Planning. 11. Act as content manager for assigned websites. Coordinate with College Relations to create, manage and maintain content for conference services and social media. 12. Act as the building manager for the Student Center. Secondary Duties: 1. Coordinate with the Chadron Chamber of Commerce and local businesses/organizations to identify community needs for conference and event space and create a positive awareness of the spaces available for rent at Chadron State College. 2. Promote conference services to potential clients in education associations, youth activities, government agencies, schools as well as business, industry, civic and service organizations. 3.Direct the conferencing efforts for the satisfaction of client needs while utilizing campus facilities. 4. Maintain effective budget control for the Conferencing Office. 5. Recruit, train, supervise and assign duties to full and/or part-time conference staff. 6. Provide support (ticket sales, mailings and deposits) to the Post Playhouse as needed. 7. Other duties as assigned by supervisor. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Preferred Qualifications Experience in event coordination and management. Strong organizational and detail-oriented skills. Excellent verbal, written and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to work weekends and evening hours as necessary. Bilingual – Spanish speaking. Physical Demands The physical requirements for this position may include, but are not necessarily limited to, the ability to use a computer, calculator, telephone, keyboard, and/or various types of office equipment. Must be able to effectively communicate in verbal and written formats and satisfactorily perform the functions of this position. License and Certification Requirements None Other Requirements Successful background records and credit check Valid driver’s license Satisfactory evaluation of driving record Salary Information $46,491-$58,114 FTE 1.000 FLSA Exempt Union Status NSCPA Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1661P Desired Start Date 05/11/2026 Open Date 04/23/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants General Information EEO Statement The Nebraska State Colleges are equal opportunity institutions and prohibit unlawful discrimination and harassment. Each College has designated an individual to coordinate the Colleges’ non-discrimination efforts to comply with regulations implementing Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination Act of 1975, and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies and practices may be directed to the Compliance Coordinators assigned at each College and identified on each College website. Veteran Statement This position is subject to Veterans Preference. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you now or will you in the future require sponsorship to work in the United States? Yes No * This position requires the individual to work in Chadron, NE.  Are you willing and able to relocate if you do not already live in the area? Yes No * Do you have a bachelor's degree? Yes No * This position requires occasional evening and weekend are you available to work evening and weekends? Yes No * Are you bilingual/Spanish-speaking? Yes No * Please give us an example of an event you coordinated or a project you saw through to completion and describe how you were able to use your organizational and planning abilities in that task. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe in detail your experience providing computer support to others and include your approach to customer service. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe in detail how your background and experience would be applicable for this position in a College/University setting. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcript 1 Optional Documents Transcript 2 Nebraska State College System Student Employment at CSC Student Employment at PSC Student Employment at WSC Chadron State College Peru State College Wayne State College To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://nscs.peopleadmin.com/postings/13460": {
      "title": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Director of Major Gifts",
      "description": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Director of Major Gifts Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About NSCS About CSC About PSC About WSC Director of Major Gifts All applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without sponsorship. Applications received after interviews are scheduled may not be fully considered for this position. We do not accept references or other application materials from outside credential management organizations. Application materials and references must be submitted through our applicant tracking system. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, please send a cover letter and resume to foundation@csc.edu . Please use “CSF Director of Major Gifts” in the subject line Posting Details Position Information Job Title Director of Major Gifts Nature of Work • The Chadron State Foundation supports Chadron State College by securing and stewarding private support that advances student success, academic excellence, and institutional strength in western Nebraska and beyond. • The Director of Major Gifts supports the Chadron State Foundation’s work to enhance Chadron State College’s ability to meet its primary educational mission in western Nebraska through fundraising activities that provide resources vital to the mission of Chadron State College in the areas of instruction, research, service, and scholarship programs. • Increase major gift revenue by transforming interest into investment. Lead a focused portfolio and a steady rhythm of small, purposeful gatherings that surface prospects, deepen relationships, and move proposals to “yes,” while keeping the CEO focused on the very top prospects. • Salary is commensurate with experience. The Chadron State Foundation may hire this position at the Associate Director, Director, or Senior Director level based on the selected candidate’s qualifications and experience. Examples of Work Performed Essential Duties: • Proactively build, manage, and own a major gifts and leadership annual giving portfolio, ensuring regular, meaningful interactions and up-to-date information in the Foundation’s donor database. • Personalize the Foundation’s story by sharing clear, tailored cases for support that match each donor’s interests and the College’s priorities. • Strategically plan and travel regionally around donor potential and alumni hotspots, including occasional nights and weekends. • Establish clear funding priorities each semester with academic partners, athletic partners, and College Relations. • Surface planned giving intent for bequests and beneficiaries, document soft commitments, and tee up technical follow-through with the CEO and Finance team. • Accurately document gift activities by preparing proposals and intent notes while collaborating with Stewardship to coordinate donor naming, benefits, and recognition. • Partner with Finance to assess and document the value of athletic and corporate donor benefits, ensuring compliance with sponsorship regulations and tax guidelines. • Facilitate meaningful donor engagement activities that lead to new connections and giving opportunities. • Prepare clear handoffs to the CEO for top prospects, including donor background, strategy, next steps, and follow-through. • Provide timely, accurate reporting that helps leadership track progress and plan strategically. • Complete additional duties as assigned. Secondary Duties: • Support donor-driven outreach that prioritizes meaningful connections and makes giving simple, clear, and rewarding. • Work as part of a collaborative team by sharing knowledge, aligning efforts, and celebrating success. • Ensure donor meetings, events, and follow-up actions lead to clear next steps. • Test new ideas, improve donor engagement practices, and help scale what works. Required Qualifications • Bachelor’s degree or equivalent combination of education and experience. • Strong communication skills in a variety of settings. • Strong relationship-building skills and comfort engaging donors, alumni, community members, or other external partners. • Strong time management and organizational skills. • Ability to support or coordinate donor meetings, small gatherings, outreach, events, communications, or other relationship-based work. • Ability to learn fundraising systems, donor communications tools, and donor reporting processes. • Sound judgment in handling confidential donor information, internal coordination, and public-facing communications. • Ability to travel regionally to meet with prospective donors. • Comfort working in a small-shop environment where fundraising, communications, events, and operations are closely connected. • Comfort working in both strategy and execution. Preferred Qualifications •        Experience managing donor relationships and personal solicitations. •        Experience supporting, coordinating, or leading major gifts, leadership annual giving, donor relations, alumni engagement, nonprofit fundraising, community outreach, sponsorships, events, or related advancement work. •        Experience facilitating small-group donor, alumni, community, or volunteer gatherings. •        Experience with a fundraising CRM . •        Experience with online giving platforms or community outreach tools. •        Experience with proposal preparation, donor documentation, planned giving conversations, sponsorships, or donor benefit tracking. •        Experience working in higher education, nonprofit fundraising, alumni relations, communications, marketing, events, or advancement services. None Physical Demands License and Certification Requirements Other Requirements • Successful background records check. • Valid driver’s license. • Satisfactory evaluation of driving record. Salary Information Salary is commensurate with experience. The Chadron State Foundation may hire this position at the Associate Director, Director, or Senior Director level based on the selected candidate’s qualifications and experience. FTE 1.000 FLSA Exempt Union Status Non-Union Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1712P Desired Start Date 09/01/2026 Open Date 07/27/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants To apply, please send a cover letter and resume to foundation@csc.edu . Please use “CSF Director of Major Gifts” in the subject line General Information About The Chadron State Foundation The Chadron State Foundation is dedicated to enhancing Chadron State College’s ability to meet its primary educational mission in western Nebraska through undertaking fundraising activities that provide resources vital to the mission of Chadron State College in the areas of instruction, research, service, and scholarship programs. EEO Statement The Chadron State Foundation is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. This means that the company will extend equal opportunity without discrimination or harassment to all individuals without regard for race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, marital status, citizenship, national origin, genetic information, handicaps, veteran’s status, or any other characteristic protected by law. This policy affirms CSF’s commitment to the principles of fair employment and to eliminating all vestiges of discriminatory practices. CSF encourages all employees to take advantage of opportunities for promotion as they occur. CSF prohibits any such discrimination or harassment Veteran Statement Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Nebraska State College System Student Employment at CSC Student Employment at PSC Student Employment at WSC Chadron State College Peru State College Wayne State College To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://nscs.peopleadmin.com/postings/13562": {
      "title": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Assistant Director - Admissions",
      "description": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Assistant Director - Admissions Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About NSCS About CSC About PSC About WSC Assistant Director - Admissions All applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without sponsorship. Applications received after interviews are scheduled may not be fully considered for this position. We do not accept references or other application materials from outside credential management organizations. Application materials and references must be submitted through our applicant tracking system. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Director - Admissions Nature of Work Assist in the development and implementation of a student recruitment strategy with specialization in a focus area. Involves recruiting students, recording student data, and travel. Examples of Work Performed Develop and implement student recruitment and support strategies and assign territories for Admissions and Senior Admissions Counselors Set goals for their team and assist the Director in tracking and analyzing prospect, recruitment and student data to meet recruitment outcomes set by the college Implement student recruitment and support strategies for assigned territories or recruitment area/group. Meet enrollment goals for assigned target recruitment area Report progress of recruitment efforts on a regular basis Identify strategies for both campus-based as well as online students Identify strategies for traditional aged incoming students, as well as for non-traditional student populations Present and promote the College and the Admissions profession in a positive way Create and maintain relationships with community-based organizations as relates to focus area Coordinates and participate in recruitment events; including face to face and virtual events Plan and coordinate recruitment activities and programs including but not limited to, summer orientation, tele-counseling, and group visits Counsel with prospective students and their families to encourage campus visits as well as apply for admission Develop an effective working relationship with community college staff Maintain appropriate follow-up communication with students regarding the status of their applications for admission Assist students with college application and admission process Assist with new student registration programs Extensive travel, evening, and weekend hours required Other duties as assigned Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree 2 years’ experience in admissions, sales, or working with diverse, first generation, and/or underrepresented populations or a combination of these areas totaling 2 years. Willingness to travel to regional areas. Preferred Qualifications Strong cross-cultural interpersonal and writing skills Public speaking skills that include experience with diverse populations Experience in college admissions, public relations Physical Demands License and Certification Requirements None Other Requirements Successful background records check Valid driver’s license Satisfactory evaluation of driving record Salary Information $47,000-$56,585 FTE 1.000 FLSA Exempt Union Status Non-Union Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1727P Desired Start Date 09/14/2026 Open Date 08/27/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants General Information EEO Statement The Nebraska State Colleges are equal opportunity institutions and prohibit unlawful discrimination and harassment. Each College has designated an individual to coordinate the Colleges’ non-discrimination efforts to comply with regulations implementing Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination Act of 1975, and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies and practices may be directed to the Compliance Coordinators assigned at each College and identified on each College website. Veteran Statement This position is subject to Veterans Preference. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you now or will you in the future require sponsorship to work in the United States? Yes No * Do you have a bachelor's degree? Yes No * Are you available to work on the Chadron State College campus? Yes No * Are you willing to travel and work a flexible schedule? Yes No * Do you have 2 years’ experience in admissions, sales, or working with diverse, first generation, and/or underrepresented populations or a combination of experience/work totaling 2 years? Yes, two or more years in admissions Yes, Two or more years in sales Yes, two or more years experience working with diverse, first generation and/or underrepresented populations Yes, more than two years exprience in combination No * Do you have a valid Driver's License or the ability to obtain one? Yes No * Please describe any supervisory work experience that you have. (Open Ended Question) * Please give us an example of an event you coordinated or a project you saw through to completion and describe how you were able to use your organizational and planning abilities in that task. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcript 1 Optional Documents Nebraska State College System Student Employment at CSC Student Employment at PSC Student Employment at WSC Chadron State College Peru State College Wayne State College To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://nscs.peopleadmin.com/postings/13323": {
      "title": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Office Assistant III",
      "description": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Office Assistant III Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About NSCS About CSC About PSC About WSC Office Assistant III All applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without sponsorship. Applications received after interviews are scheduled may not be fully considered for this position. We do not accept references or other application materials from outside credential management organizations. Application materials and references must be submitted through our applicant tracking system. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Office Assistant III Nature of Work This is an advanced classification that performs specialized clerical work of an administrative nature of varied scope and complexity requiring a broad knowledge of standardized policies and procedures, and confidentiality in the disposition of work matters. Work requires significant independent judgment, problem solving, and decision-making skills within prescribed limitations. Interprets guidelines to specific situations that are not covered by policies or procedures. Work includes the maintenance of various record systems, the creation of reports involving payroll, employee, student, departmental records, and statistical data. Work also includes composing routine memoranda, correspondence and written materials requiring knowledge of institutional policies and procedures, scheduling meetings, and making travel arrangements. Limited leadership may be exercised over small teams of co-workers or student employees. Occasional supervision and oversight is provided to employees in this classification. Examples of Work Performed Essential Duties: 1. Manages the daily office operations and provides administrative support for the Vice President Administration and Finance ( VPAF ) office as assigned. Completes assignments independently unless VPAF action is needed. 2. Assists the VPAF with state and federal compliance issues including but not limited to: Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ) – campus and building access issues Nebraska Department of Water, Energy, and Environment ( DWEE ) – Annual Air Emissions report and Operation Permit- for heating plant (every 5 years). Maintains Chlorofluorocarbon Refrigerants ( CFC ) records – HVAC leaks Maintains Hazardous material records including Safety Data Sheets, chemical inventories, hazardous waste 3.Schedules facility inspections and follows up on any required repairs: Semiannual: hood cleaning/inspection and fire alarm inspections Annual: fire sprinkler, fume hoods, fuel tanks, fire hydrants and elevator inspections Biennial: internal combustion inspection 4.Monitors construction and contingency maintenance projects in coordination with the VPAF and Assistant to VPAF , processes invoices for payment and tracks budget (including campus projects’ timelines and funding sources). 5.Responsible for board report preparation related to Capital Construction quarterly report, Auxiliary Maintenance and Progress reports, and LB 309 status reports. 6.Coordinates various insurance renewal responses process with the VPAF , college personnel, and System Office. 7.Plans and coordinates campus visits such as Fiscal Analyst, Task Force for Building Renewal (LB 309) and other high-ranking officials. Secondary Duties: 1. Other job-related duties as assigned by the immediate supervisor Required Qualifications High School diploma or equivalent College coursework in Business Administration or related field and/or two years of clerical experience Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of current office practices and procedures. Knowledge of financial systems and software used for word processing, spreadsheet and database applications. Knowledge of basic budgeting and accounting principles and practices. Skill in the operation of a computer, scanner, copier, printer, and other common office equipment. Ability to perform advanced clerical tasks and projects including composing, preparing and disseminating correspondence, reports and memoranda. Ability to communicate effectively in verbal and written formats. Ability to maintain varied filing systems and records. Physical Demands License and Certification Requirements None Other Requirements Successful background records check Salary Information $40,158-$46,500 FTE 1.000 FLSA Non-Exempt Union Status Non-Union Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1672P Desired Start Date 07/01/2026 Open Date 05/29/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants General Information EEO Statement The Nebraska State Colleges are equal opportunity institutions and prohibit unlawful discrimination and harassment. Each College has designated an individual to coordinate the Colleges’ non-discrimination efforts to comply with regulations implementing Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination Act of 1975, and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies and practices may be directed to the Compliance Coordinators assigned at each College and identified on each College website. Veteran Statement This position is subject to Veterans Preference. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This position requires the individual to work in Chadron, NE. Are you available to work on the Chadron State College campus? Yes No * Do you now or will you in the future require sponsorship to work in the United States? Yes No * Do you have a high school diploma or equivalent? Yes No * Do you have college coursework in Business Administration or a related field and/or two years of clerical experience? Yes, college course work in Business Administration or related field. Yes, two or more years of clerical experience Yes, both No * Please explain your experience with Word, Excel, and Outlook email. (Open Ended Question) * Explain your understanding of confidentiality. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Transcript 1 Transcript 2 Nebraska State College System Student Employment at CSC Student Employment at PSC Student Employment at WSC Chadron State College Peru State College Wayne State College To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
