    "https://nscs.peopleadmin.com/postings/13512": {
      "title": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Office Assistant II",
      "description": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Office Assistant II Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About NSCS About CSC About PSC About WSC Office Assistant II All applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without sponsorship. Applications received after interviews are scheduled may not be fully considered for this position. We do not accept references or other application materials from outside credential management organizations. Application materials and references must be submitted through our applicant tracking system. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Office Assistant II Nature of Work This is an advanced classification that performs complex clerical and reception work involving common office practices and procedures and requiring knowledge of standardized policies and procedures and confidentiality in the disposition of work matters. Work requires some independent judgment, problem solving, and minor decision making skills based on established policies and guidelines. Performs varied tasks such as maintaining and processing employee or student records and information and reception and clerical support for the office or department. Work includes producing reports and documents from rough draft or verbal instruction; transcribing and distributing meeting minutes; and coordinating appointments, meetings and travel arrangements. Limited leadership may be exercised over small teams of co-workers or student employees. General supervision and oversight is provided to employees in this classification. Examples of Work Performed Essential Duties: Coordinate documentation, filing, and all maintenance of medical records and insurance forms completed by Athletic Trainers for student athletes. Upload documents and gather additional information for insurance claims with multiple providers. Accesses various forms of information in order to compose, type and prepare routine correspondence, reports, forms and related materials. Including assisting all athletic staff with processing AP forms and other routine forms. Reviews and monitors operational forms for accuracy and compliance with established guidelines; generates or produces reports and documents; records, transcribes and distributes meeting minutes. Answers general and operational requests for information either in person or over the telephone; greets and directs visitors, students and staff; receives and routes correspondence and messages; opens, sorts and distributes mail. Maintains office files, records and inventory of supplies; prepares hiring forms for student workers or part-time temp employees. Assist Athletic Director with scheduling and time approval for student workers. Compiles and summarizes information and prepares standard forms and routine reports. Other duties as assigned by supervisor. Required Qualifications Graduation from High School or educational equivalent and related experience. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of current office practices and procedures Skill in the operation of a computer, scanner, copier, printer and other common office equipment. Ability to maintain accurate records, filing systems, and financial data. Ability to perform routine clerical tasks including the preparation of correspondence, reports and spreadsheets. Ability to communicate effectively in verbal and written formats. Ability to train, schedule, and guide the work of other clerical staff or student employees. Physical Demands License and Certification Requirements None Other Requirements Successful background and credit check Salary Information $37,587-$39,467 FTE 1.000 FLSA Non-Exempt Union Status NAPE Number of Vacancies Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1714P Desired Start Date 09/01/2026 Open Date 08/06/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants General Information EEO Statement The Nebraska State Colleges are equal opportunity institutions and prohibit unlawful discrimination and harassment. Each College has designated an individual to coordinate the Colleges’ non-discrimination efforts to comply with regulations implementing Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination Act of 1975, and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies and practices may be directed to the Compliance Coordinators assigned at each College and identified on each College website. Veteran Statement This position is subject to Veterans Preference. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you available to work on the Chadron State College campus? Yes No * Have you received a high school diploma or a GED? Yes No * Do you now or will you in the future require sponsorship to work in the United States? Yes No * Describe your previous experience and knowledge working with Collegiate Athletics? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Transcript 1 Transcript 2 Nebraska State College System Student Employment at CSC Student Employment at PSC Student Employment at WSC Chadron State College Peru State College Wayne State College To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://nscs.peopleadmin.com/postings/13375": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Admissions Counselor Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About NSCS About CSC About PSC About WSC Admissions Counselor All applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without sponsorship. Applications received after interviews are scheduled may not be fully considered for this position. We do not accept references or other application materials from outside credential management organizations. Application materials and references must be submitted through our applicant tracking system. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. When creating a hiring proposal please use position number 660171 for the second hire. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Admissions Counselor Nature of Work Recruit and counsel prospective students regarding the admissions and enrollment process. Report and track student admissions information. Includes extensive travel. Examples of Work Performed • Manage assigned recruiting territory from an office in Chadron, Nebraska. • Extensive travel to high schools, community colleges, college fairs, job fairs, community events and other promotional events within assigned recruiting territory. • Identify and recruit both campus based as well as online prospective students. • Plan and conduct visits to high schools, community colleges, college fairs, job fairs, community events and other promotional events • Contacts prospective students (leads) and provides accurate and complete information about the Campus and the programs of education, both undergraduate and graduate as well as campus based and online students, offered by CSC in a factual and ethical manner. • Manage and organize inquiries received for both campus based and online learners. • Take inquiry calls from all potential students interested in knowing or receiving information about CSC campus based and online programs. Make outbound phone calls to potential students that have expressed interest in attending the Campus or taking online courses. • Return web inquiries and calls promptly to all potential students. • Compose and send personal email and written correspondence • Assists applicants in completing application and enrollment paperwork, and executes such paperwork accurately and in a timely manner • Excellent knowledge of software preferably including experience with student information systems • Review EMP queries for status of pre-applicants and applicants • Maintain a social media presence • Assist in developing prospective student publications and promotional displays • Contribute ideas and provide input regarding advertising opportunities • Seek out opportunities for CSC promotional displays in assigned territory • Contribute ideas and provide input regarding the viewbook • Provide enrollment assistance to new and current students • Provide general information to prospective students, counselors, advisors and parent about CSC housing, scholarships, health services, tutoring, advising and other campus offices • Assist with tours, open houses, On-Campus Registration sessions and New Student Orientation as need Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or related work experience. Preferred Qualifications Experience in college admissions or public relations preferred Public speaking experience Computer, database and analytical skills preferred. Physical Demands License and Certification Requirements Valid driver’s license required. Other Requirements Successful background records check Satisfactory evaluation of driving record Salary Information $41,557 FTE 1.000 FLSA Non-Exempt Union Status NSCPA Number of Vacancies 2 Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1684P Desired Start Date 07/06/2026 Open Date 06/24/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants When creating a hiring proposal please use position number 660171 for the second hire. General Information EEO Statement The Nebraska State Colleges are equal opportunity institutions and prohibit unlawful discrimination and harassment. Each College has designated an individual to coordinate the Colleges’ non-discrimination efforts to comply with regulations implementing Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination Act of 1975, and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies and practices may be directed to the Compliance Coordinators assigned at each College and identified on each College website. Veteran Statement This position is subject to Veterans Preference. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor's degree or related work experience? Yes, a Bachelor's degree Yes, related work experience Yes, both No * Do you have a valid Driver's License or the ability to obtain one? Yes No * Are you available to work on the Chadron State College campus? Yes No * Do you now or will you in the future require sponsorship to work in the United States? Yes No * Please describe any previous experience you have with public speaking, including working with diverse population. (Open Ended Question) * What strengths do you have that would relate to undergraduate student recruitment?  List these in an order of importance to the posted role. (Open Ended Question) * Explain the importance of the ability to establish and maintain cooperative working relationships with a wide variety of people. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcript 1 Optional Documents Transcript 2 Nebraska State College System Student Employment at CSC Student Employment at PSC Student Employment at WSC Chadron State College Peru State College Wayne State College To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://nscs.peopleadmin.com/postings/13514": {
      "title": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Graduate Assistant E-Sports",
      "description": "Nebraska State College System - Chadron, Peru, and Wayne State | Graduate Assistant E-Sports Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About NSCS About CSC About PSC About WSC Graduate Assistant E-Sports All applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without sponsorship. Applications received after interviews are scheduled may not be fully considered for this position. We do not accept references or other application materials from outside credential management organizations. Application materials and references must be submitted through our applicant tracking system. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Graduate Assistant E-Sports Nature of Work Graduate Assistants are hired at Chadron State College to assist in meeting the vision and goals established for CSC . Strategic deployment of graduate assistant positions is essential to ensure that limited resources are utilized in a manner consistent with the philosophy of CSC . Graduate assistants provide experiential learning in select areas and to assist the individual in a successful transition to future educational and professional opportunities. Examples of Work Performed Coaching & Student-Athlete Development Plan, organize, and conduct practices. Develop individual and team strategies for all competitive titles. Recruiting & Retention Identify, recruit, and retain qualified student-athletes. Build relationships with high school esports clubs and recruiting networks. Program Administration Manage the daily operations of the esports program. Develop competition schedules and coordinate league participation. Organize team travel when applicable. Required Qualifications Completed Bachelor’s degree Conditionally accepted or accepted application to CSC graduate program Ability to work on the Chadron State College main campus Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands License and Certification Requirements Other Requirements Successful background records check Valid driver’s license Salary Information $5,760 per semester plus tuition waiver (student fees not included) FTE 0 FLSA Exempt Union Status Non-Union Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1720P Desired Start Date 08/24/2026 Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants General Information EEO Statement The Nebraska State Colleges are equal opportunity institutions and prohibit unlawful discrimination and harassment. Each College has designated an individual to coordinate the Colleges’ non-discrimination efforts to comply with regulations implementing Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination Act of 1975, and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies and practices may be directed to the Compliance Coordinators assigned at each College and identified on each College website. Veteran Statement This position is subject to Veterans Preference. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you conditionally accepted or eligible to be accepted to a Chadron State College Master's Program? Yes No * Are you available to work on the Chadron State College campus? Yes No * How do you prioritize daily tasks? (Open Ended Question) * Describe your coaching experience and philosophy. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcript 1 Optional Documents Nebraska State College System Student Employment at CSC Student Employment at PSC Student Employment at WSC Chadron State College Peru State College Wayne State College To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
